{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your scheduled IVIG infusion, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:45:12",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I come in every two weeks for this. It helps with my immune system, but it can be rough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:46:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve been on a half-dose regimen now for a few months. Can you tell me what kind of side effects you usually get?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:47:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Usually, about 12 hours after, I get chest tightness, shortness of breath, and feel like I’m going to heave the next morning. It’s delayed, not right during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:48:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll monitor you closely. You also mentioned something about an episode at home yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:50:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes — power went out, no heat. I felt the cold get to me. My heart started skipping, then slowed down. I almost passed out, but it only lasted about 15 seconds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:51:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds scary. But you recovered on your own, no chest pain or lasting symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:52:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it passed quickly. But I’ve had heart issues before — stents, SVT. And with my mitochondrial disease, my autonomic system doesn’t regulate well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:53:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. That makes you more sensitive to temperature and stress. We’ll keep you on telemetry to watch your heart rhythm during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:54:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. I also get tingling in my hands sometimes during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:55:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll slow the rate if that happens. Tingling can be a mild reaction to IVIG. We’ll premedicate you with Benadryl and Tylenol to help prevent reactions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:56:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And I’ve already had two liters of saline overnight — helps with the orthostatic hypotension."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:57:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your usual IV fluids. Your vitals now are stable — BP 130 over 86, pulse 76, oxygen 98% on room air. You’re looking good so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-03-27 15:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’m glad I’m not having fever or chills this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-03-27 16:00:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of infection today. Labs from this morning are normal — white count, kidney function, electrolytes all stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-03-27 16:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My main concern is getting through the infusion without too much trouble."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-03-27 16:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re set up for that. We’ll start the IVIG in about 30 minutes after your premeds. We’ll go slow and watch you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-03-27 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve taken your Benadryl and Tylenol. We’re starting the Gammagard infusion now at a low rate — 15 grams total."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-03-27 16:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I feel it starting. Nothing unusual yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now? It’s been about 45 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m starting to feel a little short of breath. And my chest feels tight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your oxygen level is 96%, so you’re not hypoxic. I’ll put you on 2 liters of oxygen through a nasal cannula to help you feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That already helps. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also slow the infusion rate. Let’s see if that reduces your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m also noticing a tingling in my fingers again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:22:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common and often improves when we slow the rate. We’re doing that now. Any numbness in your face or lips?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just hands."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-03-27 17:24:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. No signs of a serious allergic reaction. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-03-27 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re halfway through, and your symptoms seem to be improving. Oxygen is helping, and the tingling has lessened."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-03-27 18:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel more comfortable now. The chest tightness is much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-03-27 19:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news — the infusion is complete. You tolerated it well, all things considered. We’ll keep you on oxygen for a bit longer and monitor you overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-03-27 19:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad it’s over. I’ll probably feel tired tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-03-27 19:47:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Rest up. We’ll check on you through the night. Your heart rhythm has been stable on telemetry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. No chest tightness, no shortness of breath. I did feel a little queasy this morning, but it passed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common — part of your delayed reaction. But since you’re otherwise feeling well, and your vitals are stable, we can plan for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. No changes to my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:04:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None. You stayed on your home medications — aspirin, Plavix, metoprolol, atorvastatin, valsartan, Nexium, and the others. We just monitored you during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll keep getting IV fluids three times a week at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:07:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. And your next IVIG is in two weeks. We recommend continuing hospital admission for those infusions given your reaction history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:08:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I feel safer here during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:09:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send discharge instructions to your primary team. Follow up with Dr. ___ for your immunodeficiency and cardiology as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:10:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-03-28 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have the nurse finalize discharge paperwork. You should be out by mid-morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you’re still feeling well this morning? No new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, still feeling back to normal. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your discharge exam shows stable vitals — pulse 56, BP 142 over 80, oxygen 97% on room air. Lungs clear, heart regular."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. I’ll keep an eye on how I feel over the next day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop chest pain, severe shortness of breath, or pass out, go to the ER. Otherwise, keep to your routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. I’ll be careful with temperature changes — that cold episode scared me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. Stay warm, hydrated, and listen to your body. We’ll see you next infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-03-29 00:09:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. You’re cleared for discharge."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-03-27 15:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-03-29 12:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with mitochondrial disease, autonomic dysfunction, coronary artery disease, and hypogammaglobulinemia was admitted for observation during a scheduled biweekly IVIG infusion. He reported a brief episode of near-syncope at home triggered by cold exposure, but was asymptomatic on admission. The IVIG infusion was administered with premedication and IV fluids. During the infusion, he developed mild chest tightness, shortness of breath, and hand tingling, which improved with oxygen and slowing the infusion rate. Symptoms resolved post-infusion, and he remained hemodynamically stable without hypoxia or arrhythmias. He was monitored on telemetry and observed overnight. No medication changes were made. He was discharged home in stable condition with plans to continue outpatient IVIG and follow-up with specialists.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypogammaglobulinemia, unspecified",
      "Disorders of mitochondrial metabolism",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Other respiratory abnormalities",
      "Disturbance of skin sensation",
      "Gamma globulin causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Other specified cardiac dysrhythmias",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
